// RUN: cd %corpus && ! %zomc compile --check 08-adt/inherent_method_body_capability_neg_01.zom > %t 2>&1
// RUN: %FileCheck %s --input-file %t

// The flat scalar-literal method body now builds verified semantic HIR and
// Built MIR, but a method that returns an ordinary parameter is still outside
// the admitted scalar shape, so semantic HIR rejects the method definition
// with the per-definition capability rejection ZOM4099, not an internal
// compiler error. Receiver calls and `this` reads use the more specific
// ZOM4125 at the checker.

// CHECK-LITERAL: Error [ZOM4099]: this function body uses a construct the compiler cannot generate code for yet
// CHECK-LITERAL:   --> conformance/08-adt/inherent_method_body_capability_neg_01.zom:3:3
